# The built plugin packages are tracked: the toolbox deploys from packages/ by
# symlink, so the artifacts a build produces are what opencode runs, and a diff
# against them is the review of what actually shipped. The swap above is why:
# build-packages.mjs renames packages/ to .packages-backup/ and then moves
# .packages-tmp/ into place, so a build that fails in between leaves packages/
# absent — tracked, that is a `git checkout` to undo rather than a rebuild.
# Keep .packages-tmp/ and .packages-backup/ ignored either way; they only exist
# during a build.

ISSUES.md
.superpowers/

# Personal working notes, not part of the published plugin pack.
PLUGIN-*.md
.scratch/

# Runtime artifact of the opencode-sessions plugin. Empty in git and never
# needed by the repo: the plugin's peer state lives in ctx.storage, and any DB
# that ever lands here is local session data that must never be committed.
.opencode-sessions/
